{"c":[],"e":[[4,4,"<b>perfect</b> </p> <p> mature and complete. <i>(See Scofield \"<a data-ref=\"Matt.5.48\">Matthew 5:48</a>\")</i>."],[14,14,"<b>tempted</b></p> <p> \"Temptation\" is used in two senses:</p> <ul> <li>(1) Solicitation to evil (e.g. <a data-ref=\"Gen.3.1-Gen.3.6\">Genesis 3:1-6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Matt.4.1\">Matthew 4:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"1Cor.10.13\">1 Corinthians 10:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"2Cor.11.3\">2 Corinthians 11:3,4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jas.1.14\">James 1:14</a>).</li> <li>(2) Testing under trial (eg) <a data-ref=\"Gen.22.1\">Genesis 22:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Luke.22.28\">Luke 22:28</a> Cf <a data-ref=\"Luke.4.2\">Luke 4:2,</a> Cf <a data-ref=\"Matt.6.13\">Matthew 6:13</a> (solicitation to evil) and <a data-ref=\"1Pet.1.6\">1 Peter 1:6</a> (testing under trial)."],[15,15,"<b>sin</b> Sin.</p> <p><i>(See Scofield \"<a data-ref=\"Rom.3.23\">Romans 3:23</a>\")</i>."],[17,17,"<b>gift</b></p> <p> Two words are used in the original for \"gift,\" the first meaning the act of giving; the second, the thing given."],[20,20,"<b>righteousness</b></p> <p><i>(See Scofield \"<a data-ref=\"Rom.3.21\">Romans 3:21</a>\")</i>."],[21,21,"<b>save</b></p> <p><i>(See Scofield \"<a data-ref=\"Rom.1.16\">Romans 1:16</a>\")</i>."],[26,26,"<b>religious</b></p> <p> (Greek - θρη̑σκος = outwardly religious)."],[27,27,"<b>world</b> </p> <p> \"kosmos\" = world-system. <a data-ref=\"Jas.4.4\">James 4:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"John.7.7\">John 7:7</a> <i>(See Scofield \"<a data-ref=\"Rev.13.8\">Revelation 13:8</a>\")</i>"]]}